WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.590
Henry Cavill's fans aren't the only ones who
are thirsty.

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:07.720
The new face of Geralt of Rivia recently sat
down with Graham Norton back in his native

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.660
England to talk about his role on Netflix's
The Witcher.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.950
The scene everyone was desperate for after
the first Witcher trailer arrived - the monster-hunting

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.290
Geralt sitting in that famous wooden bathtub,
naked as the day he was born - was the big

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:23.430
clip featured during Cavill's interview with
Norton, and that naturally invited questions

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.430
about how he prepared for The Witcher's most
famous scene.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:30.590
Fans are at least casually familiar in this
age of Thors and Supermen that the diet required

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:35.120
to maintain a perfectly sculpted brickhouse
physique is punishing and mostly comprised

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.090
of eating one's weight in boneless, skinless
chicken breasts.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:42.380
Chatting with Norton about how he got ready
to portray Geralt, Cavill revealed a new twist

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:47.370
in the horror-show that putting perfect bodies
on film necessitates: purposefully dehydrating

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.899
himself over several days.

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:52.890
Cavill explained that the worst part about
playing Geralt was the sharp decline in fluid

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.000
intake he had to endure to get ready for all
the shirtless scenes.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.000
He told Norton,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.280
"On the first day, you'll have, like a liter
and a half [of water], the second day a half-liter,

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:04.280
and then the third day, no water, and you'll
shoot on the fourth."

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.890
He went on to say that by the time he's done
shooting on that fourth day, he's, quote,

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.350
"the most miserable person on Earth."

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.350
"Bleh!

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.260
Dry mouth!"

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.280
But why, though?

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.310
Isn't putting Cavill through an incredibly
bland and utilitarian diet for months on end

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.850
for the sake of vanity enough?

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:23.490
"It makes your skin really thin, so it sits
on the muscles."

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:27.420
This method of purposeful dehydration is a
common one for bodybuilders preparing for

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:32.500
competition or photoshoots, boxers and MMA
fighters trying to drop pounds before weigh-ins,

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.500
and actors alike.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:37.780
Sure, Cavill is still massive in size and
could probably crush a watermelon between

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:42.530
his bicep and forearm, but the high-definition
cut of his musculature requires tricking the

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:43.530
body temporarily.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:48.330
Warning: We don't recommend trying any of
this without medical supervision!

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:52.369
Dehydrating is the final step in the process
towards a temporary period of maximum muscle

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:55.590
definition, and bodybuilders refer to it as
"peak day."

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:59.920
The first stage, about two weeks before the
target date, requires temporarily increasing

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.000
your sodium consumption, which tricks the
body's usual water retention ratio.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.119
At first, it will retain water, but eventually
re-adapt and normalize.

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:12.660
When sodium intake is severely cut a week
later, water will rapidly exit the body along

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:17.650
with it, meaning there's almost no added water
weight or possible bloating because of it.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.090
Along with this process, consumption of carbs
are cut to almost nothing.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:25.310
This temporarily supercharges burning the
minuscule amount of excess fat left in the

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.310
body.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:30.190
It's a precarious balancing act to increasingly
deprive yourself of water, and yet give your

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:34.060
muscles enough hydration to handle those workouts
that still have to get done.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:38.040
The skin thins for the lack of fluid within
and underneath it, giving that last little

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.040
bit of definition.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.040
At the end of all that, you get exactly one
perfect day to get slicked over with baby

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:48.060
oil and tossed into tastefully-opaque bathwater
for five minutes of sexy footage.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.629
For The Witcher, Cavill had to go through
this grueling process repeatedly for every

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:55.600
single one of the several scenes in which
he's featured shirtless, because his super-cut

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:59.379
physique can't be consistently maintained
for the weeks and weeks it takes to film a

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.540
TV series.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:04.069
You're hungry and thirsty, and when you're
not working in front of a camera, you're still

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:08.600
working off-site in a gym with an entire team
of people monitoring you down to the finest,

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.819
dehumanizing detail.

00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:14.190
Cavill said in the interview that by the end
of all those day-4 shoots, he had a peculiar

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.190
sensation.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:20.209
"You get to the point on the last day where
you can smell water, like nearby."

00:03:20.209 --> 00:03:22.130
Sounds like one of Geralt's special skills
…

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:30.120
"I smelled what you were doing!"

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.170
Bless Henry Cavill for his dedication and
patience, because this whole process sounds

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.000
like the absolute worst.

